# AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE Knowledge Base Mount

Treat `../AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE` (**AGB**) as a **mounted knowledge base** for this workspace. Read and apply its contents when planning, researching, or producing work here. Prefer its documents over inventing parallel structure.

**Abbreviation:** `AGB` = AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE. Use either form in conversation and artifacts; paths remain under the mount root.

**Resolution:** AGB is the sibling folder of the workspace root. Resolve `../AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE` against the workspace root (not against this rule file's folder), and use the resulting absolute path only at runtime for tool calls, without writing it into artifacts, docs, commits, or replies. If `../AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE` does not exist, say so to the user and ask where AGB is instead of guessing.

## Bootstrap (every session)

1. Read `AGB/AGENTS.md` first — authoritative orientation for all Type B agents.
2. Use `AGB/README.md` only as a short map if you need a directory overview.
3. Resolve paths below relative to the mount root (`../AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE` from the workspace root). Do not assume files live inside AGENT-PLAYGROUND unless they actually do.

